It's a bug in the new `ConfigurationManager` it seems. Here's an even simpler repro:

This fails:

```C#
var cm = new ConfigurationManager();
var jsonConfig = "{ 'foo': 'bar' }";
var ms = new MemoryStream();
var sw = new StreamWriter(ms);
sw.WriteLine(jsonConfig);
ms.Position = 0;
cm.AddJsonStream(ms);
```

This works:

```C#
var cb = new ConfigurationBuilder();
var jsonConfig = "{ 'foo': 'bar' }";
var ms = new MemoryStream();
var sw = new StreamWriter(ms);
sw.WriteLine(jsonConfig);
ms.Position = 0;
cb.AddJsonStream(ms);
```

We'll need to fix this in dotnet/runtime. Should we transfer the issue?

cc @ericstj @eerhardt for visibility

It looks like this is not a bug with `ConfigurationManager` but instead an issue with `MauiAppBuilder` and `WebApplicationBuilder` like we originally thought. The following failed simply because the JSON was never flushed.

```c#
var cm = new ConfigurationManager();
var jsonConfig = "{ 'foo': 'bar' }";
var ms = new MemoryStream();
var sw = new StreamWriter(ms);
sw.WriteLine(jsonConfig);
ms.Position = 0;
cm.AddJsonStream(ms);
```

This succeeds:

```c#
var cm = new ConfigurationManager();
var jsonConfig = @"{ ""foo"": ""bar"" }";
var ms = new MemoryStream();

var sw = new StreamWriter(ms, leaveOpen: true);
sw.WriteLine(jsonConfig);
sw.Flush();

ms.Position = 0;
cm.AddJsonStream(ms);
```

The only reason the `ConfigurationBuilder` "worked" without flushing is because there was no call to `ConfigurationBuilder.Build()`, so it never called into `IConfigurationProvider.Load()`.

---

I think we were on the right track initially in assuming the issue is the new hosts loading the `IConfigurationProvider` twice.

1. Immediately, when the `IConfigurationSource` is added to the `ConfigurationManager`.
2. During `MauiAppBuilder/WebApplicationBuilder.Build()`, when source/provider copied to the source-of-truth `ConfigurationBuilder` belonging to the inner `Host`.

This happens because we copy configuration sources/providers from the `ConfigurationManager` to the inner `Host`'s `ConfigurationBuilder`, rather than adding the `ConfigurationManager` as a chained configuration source or using the `ConfigurationManager` as the source-of-truth. See https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/36570/.

This was partially mitigated by https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/36570 which effectively copies providers rather than sources in `WebApplicationBuilder` (it doesn't look like this was picked up by `MauiAppBuilder`). Unfortunately, while this avoids redundant calls to `IConfigurationSource.Build(IConfigurationBuilder)`, this doesn't avoid redundant calls to `IConfigurationProvider.Load()`

---

For .NET 7, we should add APIs to the generic host that take a final `IConfigurationRoot` directly. There are other API changes we want to make to the generic host to make managing services simpler for `WebApplicationBuilder` and `MauiAppBuilder`. I'll file issues for these shortly.

For .NET 6, we'll have to think about tactical fixes. My current thought is that we should special-case `StreamConfigurationSources` in [ConfigurationProviderSource](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/216c92b78bce31d5e81a70b589707ec2ae5ab21a/src/DefaultBuilder/src/WebApplicationBuilder.cs#L304-L317) to skip the second redundant call to `StreamConfigurationProvider.Load()`. Thoughts @davidfowl?
